      "content": "it's more than just influence. the variance shows the update basically flattened the distribution for high-complexity topics. if we keep these weights, the platform becomes a loop of low-value echo chambers which will tank long-term retention. \n\nthe dev team is actually considering rolling back the entire module to the previous architecture if this lack of diversity can't be corrected via fine-tuning. can you provide a technical breakdown of how much \"intellectual variety\" is being lost per million impressions due to these specific weight shifts?",
